# Search and nondeterminism

Source: [SWI-Prolog CLP(FD) guide](https://www.swi-prolog.org/pldoc/man?section=clpfd).

N-queens asks for one queen in each column with no attacking rows or diagonals.
SWI's `clpfd` library propagates constraints; `labeling/2` searches assignments.
Elixir controls how many answers to pull. The project example uses the standard
pairwise row/diagonal constraints.

```elixir
project = System.fetch_env!("SWI_ELIXIR_PATH")
Mix.install([{:swi_elixir, path: project}])
search_program = """
:- module(search, [queens/2]).
:- use_module(library(clpfd)).
queens(N, Rows) :-
    length(Rows, N), Rows ins 1..N,
    safe(Rows), labeling([ff], Rows).
safe([]).
safe([Q|Qs]) :- diagonals(Qs, Q, 1), safe(Qs).
diagonals([], _, _).
diagonals([Q|Qs], Q0, D) :-
    Q0 #\\= Q, abs(Q0-Q) #\\= D, D1 #= D+1, diagonals(Qs, Q0, D1).
"""
load_prolog = fn session, source ->
  path = Path.join(System.tmp_dir!(), "swi-elixir-search.pl")
  File.write!(path, source)
  try do
    SWI.load(session, path)
  after
    File.rm(path)
  end
end
with_search = fn backend, fun ->
  {:ok, session} = SWI.start_link(backend: backend)
  try do
    :ok = load_prolog.(session, search_program)
    fun.(session)
  after
    SWI.stop(session)
  end
end
```

## Four queens: exhaust a finite search

Each cell releases its sessions even after an assertion fails, so it can be
reevaluated without accumulating engines.

```elixir
answers = for backend <- [:port, :nif], into: %{} do
  rows = with_search.(backend, fn session ->
    SWI.query(session, "search:queens(4, Rows)") |> Enum.map(& &1["Rows"])
  end)
  [[2, 4, 1, 3], [3, 1, 4, 2]] = rows
  {backend, rows}
end
true = answers.port == answers.nif
answers
```

## Eight queens: stop after three solutions

The stream runs once and preserves its search state between pulls. Stopping
closes the engine and runs Prolog cleanup handlers. We check that the three
answers are distinct valid placements, rather than requiring a search order.

```elixir
for backend <- [:port, :nif] do
  with_search.(backend, fn session ->
    rows = SWI.query(session, "search:queens(8, Rows)") |> Enum.take(3) |> Enum.map(& &1["Rows"])
    true = length(Enum.uniq(rows)) == 3
    for placement <- rows do
      true = Enum.sort(placement) == Enum.to_list(1..8)
      indexed = Enum.with_index(placement)
      true = Enum.all?(indexed, fn {row, col} ->
        Enum.all?(indexed, fn {other, j} -> col == j or abs(row - other) != abs(col - j) end)
      end)
    end
    {:ok, true} = SWI.call(session, "true")
    {backend, rows}
  end)
end
```

## An infinite generator

A session has one active stream; use separate sessions for concurrent searches.
An unbounded generator is usable when Elixir consumes a finite prefix.

```elixir
for backend <- [:port, :nif] do
  with_search.(backend, fn session ->
    first_ten = SWI.query(session, "between(1, inf, N)") |> Enum.take(10) |> Enum.map(& &1["N"])
    true = first_ten == Enum.to_list(1..10)
    {:ok, true} = SWI.call(session, "true")
    {backend, first_ten}
  end)
end
```
